}

ManualAcquisition: {
	WaterChestnut: 由深海生物群系自然生长的水元栗植物掉落获得
	ManaBerry: 从地表神圣草上的魔力浆果植物上采摘获得
	Heartstriker: 在丛林生物群系钓鱼获得
	ArcaneSpike: 无法获得
	EnchantedStaff: 从地下金箱获得
	SpittingFish: 在海洋生物群系钓鱼获得
	RogueRoninHeadband: 击败史莱姆王后，在旅商处 (33.3% 概率) 售卖获得
	NoteHairpin: 在旅商处售卖获得
	HatFish: 在白天的海洋生物群系钓鱼获得
	RingofUnity: 有概率从绯红箱中获取，也可在绯红匣中获得
	AloeLeaf: 有概率从地下丛林的大型叶类植物（环境物体）掉落获得
	HeartRateMonitor: 在旅商处售卖获得
	LivingWoodSap: 在生命树中的生命木箱获得，或者挖掘树液覆盖的生命之叶灌木获得
	SeedofHope: 在生命树中的生命木箱获得
	AbyssalWhistle: 地狱任何怪物都有概率掉落获得
	FishEgg: 挖掘大珊瑚（环境物体）时掉落获得
	ExoticMynaEgg: 用任意虫网捕捉八哥时获得
	MoleCrate: 在旅商处售卖获得
	ChiLantern: 击败邪恶BOSS后，在旅商处售卖获得
	DestinyWeaver: 无法获得
	TheGauntlet: 无法获得
	Fishbone: 在地牢的渊海箱中获得
	PharaohsSlab: 在地牢的沙漠箱中获得
	PhoenixStaff: 在地牢的地狱箱中获得
	AdventurersLantern: 从地下和洞穴层的帐篷（环境物体）获得
	BrainCoral: 在猩红生物群系或猩红地下钓鱼获得
	RivetingTadpole: 在丛林生物群系钓鱼获得
	SamsaraLotus: 击败邪恶BOSS后，在旅商处售卖获得
	RottenCod: 在腐化生物群系或腐化地下钓鱼获得
	PharaohsBreath: 沙漠生物群系以及地下沙漠任何怪物都有概率掉落获得
	SoulofPlight: 困难模式下地狱任何怪物都有概率掉落获得
	FlamingCrackGut: 在岩浆中钓鱼获得
	MagmaGill: 在岩浆中钓鱼获得
	UnholyShards: 血月期间任何怪物都有概率掉落获得
}

// Make sure the text doesn't extend beyond the UI. Check the terms against the mod's translation into your language
// $parentVal is the main tab category with subcategories
// Don't translate {i:ThoriumMod/ItemName}, instead of this key, the text displays the item

InfoBook: {
	GuideDialogue: 在玩瑟银? 看来你的品味不错，给你这本瑟银信息手册--里面记录着有关这个模组各种实用指南。
	UnlockNotification: 信息手册已解锁！使用“打开信息手册”的控键即可打开。
	GuideBubble: 过来，朋友!
}

HintBook: {
	NpcTooltips: {
		ThoriumMod_TheGrandThunderBird: Use a [i:ThoriumMod/GrandFlareGun] with [i:ThoriumMod/StormFlare] during the day in the Desert.
		ThoriumMod_QueenJellyfish: Use a [i:ThoriumMod/JellyfishResonator] during the day at the Ocean.
		ThoriumMod_GraniteEnergyStorm: Use a [i:ThoriumMod/UnstableCore] deep underground within a Granite Enclosure or find and defeat an Unstable Energy Anomaly.
		ThoriumMod_BoreanStrider: Randomly appears during a Blizzard or summoned with a [i:ThoriumMod/StriderTear].
		ThoriumMod_FallenBeholder: Use a [i:ThoriumMod/VoidLens] within the Underworld.
		ThoriumMod_Viscount: Use 5 Unholy Shards at an underground Blood Chamber. Use a [i:ThoriumMod/GrimPointer] to track down the Blood Chamber.
		ThoriumMod_PatchWerk: Randomly appears during the Blood Moon. Can be resummoned with a [i:ThoriumMod/FreshBrain] purchased from the Confused Zombie. Start the Blood Moon with a [i:BloodMoonStarter].
		ThoriumMod_CorpseBloom: Randomly appears in the Underground Jungle after defeating the Eater of Worlds / Brain of Cthulhu. Can be resummoned with a [i:ThoriumMod/RottingSpore] purchased from the Confused Zombie.
		ThoriumMod_Blacksmith: Comes after defeating the Eye of Cthulhu.
		ThoriumMod_Druid: Comes after defeating the Corpse Bloom.
		ThoriumMod_ConfusedZombie: Comes after defeating the Patch Werk.
		ThoriumMod_Diverman: Comes after defeating the Queen Jellyfish.
		ThoriumMod_BuriedChampion: Use a [i:ThoriumMod/AncientBlade] deep underground within a Marble Enclosure or find and defeat a Bizarre Rock Formation.
		ThoriumMod_StarScouter: Use a [i:ThoriumMod/StarCaller] high in the sky.
		ThoriumMod_Lich: Use 30 pumpkins at the Ancient Phylactery in the graveyard beyond the Dungeon.
		ThoriumMod_ForgottenOne: Pick up 3 [i:ThoriumMod/AbyssalShadow], which are dropped by Aquatic Hallucinations in the Aquatic Depths.
		ThoriumMod_Cobbler: Comes if a player in the world has any type of shoe accessory in their inventory or equipment slots, with addition of the Aglet and Anklet of the Wind.
		ThoriumMod_Cook: Comes after defeating the King Slime.
		ThoriumMod_DesertAcolyte: Comes after defeating The Grand Thunder Bird.
	}

	Title: 瑟银信息手册
	OpenButton: 打开信息手册
	DragHint: 按住鼠标右键拖拽
	MobList.Header: "{0} — {1} ({2})"

	Tabs: {
		Basics: 瑟银模组
		EarlyGame: 模组进度
		Progression: 机制
		Bestiary: 生物
		Tips: 小贴士

		Classes: {
			$parentVal: 新职业
			Bard: 吟游诗人
			Healer: 牧师
			Thrower: 投手
		}
	}

	Basics: {
		P1: "{img:ThoriumLogo}"
		P2:
			'''
			瑟银是泰拉瑞亚最大的内容性模组之一，已开发超过 10 年。. 
			它包含大量与泰拉瑞亚原版兼容的内容，包括: 约2900件物品，约200只NPC，3只迷你BOSS，11只BOSS，1个全新的生物群
系，1个新建筑，以及大量兼容原版泰拉瑞亚的事件，生物群系等内容。
			通过这本信息手册，你无需阅读wiki即可了解该模组的基础知识 (尽管它并不能完全代替维基百科). 
			你还将找到我的个人游戏经验 (我已经通关约十次)。祝你游戏愉快!
			以上翻译来自作者，与瑟银汉化组无关。
			'''
	}

	EarlyGame: {
		P1:
			'''
			=====================================================
			In this mini-guide, you will briefly learn where and at which stages of the game you should go to find new content. 
			=====================================================
			'''
		P2:
			'''
			[c/00ff00:Start game:]
			At the very beginning of the game, you have a {i:ThoriumMod/FamilyHeirloom}Family Heirloom in your inventory. 
			At the moment it is useless; only in the endgame can it be crafted into a weak weapon for your collection. 
			It is not mentioned in the tooltip, but it grants 1 defense, so you can simply wear it until you get your first accessories.
			'''
		P3:
			'''
			Thorium has virtually no impact on the beginning of the game; you still perform the same basic actions as in vanilla, and new content will find its way to you on its own. 
			It is worth mentioning {i:ThoriumMod/ThoriumOre}Thorium Ore and {i:ThoriumMod/LifeQuartz}Life Quartz — at the start of the game these are pretty good materials. 
			Thorium Ore is used to craft decent starting armor and a very useful accessory, {i:ThoriumMod/Crietz}Crietz, which you can wear until the start of hardmode.
			'''
		P4:
			'''
			{npc:4}[c/00ff00:Post bosses:]
			After defeating {npc:ThoriumMod/TheGrandThunderBird}The Grand Thunder Bird, the {npc:4}Eye of Cthulhu, {npc:50}King Slime, and the {npc:266}{npc:13}evil boss, several modded town NPCs will arrive who sell some useful items. 
			For example, from the {npc:ThoriumMod/Blacksmith}Blacksmith you can buy the {i:ThoriumMod/ArcaneArmorFabricator}Arcane Armor Fabricator — a crafting station on which you can craft decent equipment before the evil boss. 
			Also, during a Blood Moon, the mini-boss {npc:ThoriumMod/PatchWerk}Patch Werk spawns, from which a useful {i:ThoriumMod/SuspiciousMoisturizerBottle}hand pet drops that points to rare enemies and laughs at your deaths. 
			During a Goblin Army invasion, you can obtain the {i:ThoriumMod/DarkGate}Dark Gate, also a useful item that can be used for some time.
			'''
		P5:
			'''
			{npc:266}{npc:13}[c/00ff00:Post evil boss:]
			After defeating the evil boss, you gain access to several new bosses and one new biome. 
			In the Underground Jungle, the {npc:ThoriumMod/CorpseBloom}Corpse Bloom begins to spawn; after killing it, a useful NPC, the {npc:ThoriumMod/Druid}Druid, arrives who sells plant seeds for potions. 
			Having bought a {i:ThoriumMod/GrimPointer}Grim Pointer from the {npc:ThoriumMod/ConfusedZombie}Confused Zombie, you can use it to find the {link:https://thoriummod.wiki.gg/wiki/Blood_Chamber|Blood Chamber}, in which you can summon the {npc:ThoriumMod/Viscount}Viscount using {i:ThoriumMod/UnholyShards}Unholy Shards at the {link:https://thoriummod.wiki.gg/wiki/Blood_Altar|Altar}. 
			The Viscount drops pretty good weapons and is overall a very enjoyable boss (btw my favorite boss of the mod). 
			At the ocean, you can summon the {npc:ThoriumMod/QueenJellyfish}Queen Jellyfish, from which drops... the {npc:ThoriumMod/Diverman}Diverman NPC, who makes your stay in the new biome easier. 
			Oh right, the new biome — you can now visit the {link:https://thoriummod.wiki.gg/wiki/Aquatic_Depths|Aquatic Depths}. 
			They always appear under the ocean on the Jungle side, so you won't have trouble finding them. 
			There's nothing particularly important in the biome itself, except you can check the loot in the local chests and mine {i:ThoriumMod/Aquaite}Aquaite Ore, from which various equipment is crafted. Next, Skeletron and the Queen Bee await you.
			'''
		P6:
			'''
			{npc:35}[c/00ff00:Post Skeletron:]
			After defeating Skeletron, the path to the Dungeon is open to you. 
			In the Dungeon there are several new materials of interest to you, namely {i:ThoriumMod/aDarksteelAlloy}Darksteel Ingot and {i:ThoriumMod/SpiritDroplet}Spirit Droplet. 
			In the Dungeon chests there is also new loot, you can look for it. 
			Next up are as many as 3 modded bosses — {npc:ThoriumMod/GraniteEnergyStorm}Granite Energy Storm, {npc:ThoriumMod/BuriedChampion}Buried Champion, and {npc:ThoriumMod/StarScouter}Star Scouter. 
			Granite Energy Storm doesn't particularly provide loot, but the Buried Champion drops decent {i:ThoriumMod/ChampionWing}wings before you craft hardmode ones. 
			Star Scouter drops very good weapons for all classes except Healer, and with it the Wall of Flesh won't cause problems.
			'''
		P7:
			'''
			{npc:113}[c/00ff00:Welcome to Hardmode:]
			Well then, Hardmode... from this point on, Thorium becomes much more content-rich. 
			From the chat message, you may have already guessed that new enemies have appeared in the Aquatic Depths. 
			You should pay a visit there for two new materials — {i:ThoriumMod/DepthScale}Depth Scales and {i:ThoriumMod/AbyssalChitin}Abyssal Chitin. 
			But far more important is {i:ThoriumMod/CrystalWave}Crystal Wave. Its usefulness is already clear from the tooltip. 
			It grows in the Aquatic Depths starting from the beginning of Hardmode — just break it and it will drop. Below is what it looks like.
			Don't forget to also throw one into Shimmer to obtain a permanent upgrade item.
			'''
		P8: "{img:Crystal_wave_world}"
		P9:
			'''
			Beyond the Aquatic Depths, new content also awaits you in the Pirate Invasion, the Blood Moon, the Hallow, the Underworld, the Desert, and the evil biome. 
			Each of them is notable for new materials, which in turn are used to craft starter equipment for certain classes. 
			The materials you're looking for are: {i:ThoriumMod/UnfathomableFlesh}, {i:ThoriumMod/GreenDragonScale}, {i:ThoriumMod/SoulofPlight}, {i:ThoriumMod/PharaohsBreath}, {i:ThoriumMod/HallowedCharm}, and {i:ThoriumMod/BloodCell}. 
			Check what you can craft from them and craft whatever you like.
			You can also try killing the new mimics — {npc:ThoriumMod/SubmergedMimic}, {npc:ThoriumMod/HellBringerMimic} and {npc:ThoriumMod/MyceliumMimic}. They can either spawn naturally or be summoned using keys, similar to the vanilla Keys of Light and Night.
			'''
		P10:
			'''
			{npc:ThoriumMod/FallenBeholder}[c/00ff00:First bosses:]
			Before fighting the bosses, besides standard equipment, I recommend you craft {i:ThoriumMod/DemosGuidanceItem}Demo's Guidance — it's a pet that will replace all your stationary buff tiles. 
			You can easily wear it until the end of the game; I don't know a more useful pet in Thorium. 
			Next up are two new bosses: the {npc:ThoriumMod/BoreanStrider}Borean Strider and the {npc:ThoriumMod/FallenBeholder}Fallen Beholder. Both are VERY easy and won't cause any problems. 
			The Borean Strider doesn't have impressive loot; after defeating it, new enemies will begin to spawn in the Spider Caves, but their drops aren't particularly exciting either. 
			After defeating the Fallen Beholder, however, there's something to look forward to. First, there are two new ores — {i:ThoriumMod/LodeStoneChunk}Lodestone Chunks and {i:ThoriumMod/ValadiumChunk}Valadium Chunks. 
			They spawn underground alternately after the boss is killed (i.e., the first kill spawns one ore, the second kill spawns the other, and then the cycle repeats). 
			Mine them and see what you can craft. Second, the {npc:ThoriumMod/ConfusedZombie}Confused Zombie starts selling new useful items and the material {i:ThoriumMod/VoidHeart}Void Heart, from which an interesting hook is crafted. 
			The Fallen Beholder itself drops decent weapons and a mount that can be upgraded in the endgame. After that, you just kill all the mechanical bosses.
			'''
		P11:
			'''
			{npc:134}{npc:126}{npc:127}[c/00ff00:Post mechs:]
			After defeating all three mechanical bosses, you gain access to several new materials. 
			First of all, you need to upgrade your forge by crafting the {i:ThoriumMod/SoulForge}Soul Forge, on which almost all further Thorium items are crafted. 
			Below is a list of what you can craft and why: 
			{i:ThoriumMod/SubspaceWings}Subspace Wings — good wings for the upcoming bosses. 
			{i:ThoriumMod/TimeWarp}Time Warp — if you're too lazy to skip time with a bed and you don't play with QoL mods. 
			{i:ThoriumMod/AirStrikeShield}Air Strike Shield — a very useful item if you play using only Sentries or play in co-op. 
			{i:ThoriumMod/WishingGlass}Wishing Glass — an upgrade to the Shellphone with extra teleportations. 
			{i:ThoriumMod/AromaticBulb}Aromatic Bulb — if you can't find Plantera's Bulb, it'll be easier to use its summon item. 
			{i:ThoriumMod/TitanicBar}Titanic Bar — a material. The armor made from it is shit, but the weapons are worth trying out. 
			Also, the mechs dropped {i:ThoriumMod/StrangePlating}Strange Plating and {i:ThoriumMod/LifePoweredEnergyCell}Life-Powered Energy Cell for you. From the first, a very useful — I'd even say unbalanced — weapon is crafted for the rest of the game. It literally destroys every boss all the way up to the Lunatic Cultist. 
			The second material is only useful for the Healer
			'''
		P12:
			'''
			Next, you'll have to face the {npc:ThoriumMod/Lich}Lich and {npc:262}Plantera. 
			The Lich is summoned anywhere by using pumpkins on the {i:ThoriumMod/AncientPhylactery}Ancient Phylactery. 
			It's located in the {link:https://thoriummod.wiki.gg/wiki/Natural_Graveyard|Graveyard} behind the Dungeon, but you can simply buy it from the {npc:ThoriumMod/ConfusedZombie}Confused Zombie and place it anywhere. That's even better. 
			The Lich is a very easy boss, but it deals very high damage and can regenerate HP during its second phase. To prevent the regeneration, you need to kill the {npc:ThoriumMod/PhylacteryofaThousandSouls}Phylactery of a Thousand Souls, which it periodically spawns. 
			Against this boss, it's very important to avoid contact damage and have high DPS — then you won't have any problems with it. 
			In addition to materials and weapons, the Lich drops the {i:ThoriumMod/Phylactery}Phylactery (on Expert mode), which can be placed in a vanity slot and used when needed. 
			After that, you just need to kill Plantera — with weapons made from {i:ThoriumMod/StrangePlating}Strange Plating, this boss is nothing.
			'''
		P13:
			'''
			{npc:262}[c/00ff00:Post Plantera:]
			After Plantera is defeated, {i:ThoriumMod/IllumiteChunk}Illumite becomes available. Illumite spawns in the Cavern and Underground layers, and only after Plantera's first defeat — just like Valadium and Lodestone after the Fallen Beholder, it won't spawn again on subsequent kills. 
			Illumite is used to craft mediocre Ranger armor and a couple of questionable weapons, but you can try them out if you like. 
			What should interest you far more are the changes to the Jungle Temple and the Dungeon. Both have new enemies that drop new materials — {i:ThoriumMod/SolarPebble}Solar Pebble in the Temple and {i:ThoriumMod/DarkMatter}Dark Matter in the Dungeon. 
			Also, with Ectoplasm you can upgrade several materials you're already familiar with. Check the crafting recipes yourself. 
			If you're a Healer, you can try farming Paladins for {i:ThoriumMod/HolyKnightsAlloy}Holy Knight's Alloy, which is used to craft some decent armor. 
			You can already head out to kill the new boss — the {npc:ThoriumMod/ForgottenOne}Forgotten One. There's not much to say about it: the boss itself is easy, and its drops are, to put it mildly, not very useful — except maybe for farming Healer armor and a fishing rod. 
			For now, I recommend killing Duke Fishron for the {i:ThoriumMod/SoulAnchor}Soul Anchor. The Anchor is one of the most useful items in the mod, especially if you're squeamish about healing at the Nurse. 
			Vanilla events (Solar Eclipse and moons) have also gotten a bunch of new drops, so you can farm those if you want. After that, you can kill Golem.
			'''
		P14:
			'''
			{npc:439}[c/00ff00:Pre Moon Loser:]
			The developers were a bit stingy with post-Golem content, so you'll mostly need to farm vanilla items. 
			If your crit chance is around 50–70%+, I strongly recommend crafting the {i:ThoriumMod/MaskoftheCrystalEye}Mask of the Crystal Eye (what a dumb name). If you have high crit chance, this accessory roughly increases your damage by 12–20%, since each crit deals 12% more damage and also increases the crit itself by 8%. 
			The Martian Invasion (unsurprisingly) also has new drops, both from enemies and from the flying saucer, so you can farm it if you want. 
			After that, all that's left is to go for the Lunatic Cultist.
			'''
		P15:
			'''
			A new weapon can drop from the Cultist... 3 MAGE WEAPONS FROM THE CULTIST. 
			Why? What the hell for? It doesn't even drop with a 100% chance, and the Cultist doesn't spawn until the pillars are dead — so why would you even farm him?... 
			Anyway, I dragged out this section, so now on to the content. 
			After obtaining the Ancient Manipulator, you'll be able to craft {i:ThoriumMod/TerrariumCore}Terrarium Cores. Don't be scared by their recipe — you should already have all the materials from earlier, and getting the missing ones won't be a problem. 
			From the Cores, a very good multi-class armor is crafted, which you can wear against the Moon Lord. 
			They're also used to craft weapons for every class — an excellent alternative to the Fragment weapons. 
			You can also craft {i:ThoriumMod/TerrariumWings}wings, if you didn't farm Fishron's or the Empress's wings. 
			{i:ThoriumMod/TerrariumParticleSprinters}Terrarium Boots noticeably increase your movement speed, but do you really need them when you have wings and mounts? Decide for yourself. 
			{i:ThoriumMod/TerrariumDefender}The Terrarium Defender... trash. It's not worth the farm, and it's completely useless against the last two bosses, trust me. 
			Next, kill the Pillars and craft Fragment weapons, then kill the Moon Lord.
			'''
		P16:
			'''
			{npc:ThoriumMod/DreamEater}[c/FF0000:T][c/FF7D00:H][c/FFFF00:E] [c/00FF00:P][c/0000FF:R][c/4B0082:I][c/9400D3:M][c/FF0000:O][c/FF7D00:R][c/FFFF00:D][c/00FF00:I][c/0000FF:A][c/4B0082:L][c/9400D3:S]
			Now the most interesting part begins... The Primordials are the hardest boss in Thorium... for those who haven't heard about the legendary star! The one that drops from the Moon Lord! Which, in combination with the Soaring Insignia, counters all the attacks the devs made for them, easy-peasy! 
			Anyway, on to the boss. 
			It makes sense to bring post-Moon Lord gear — armor, weapons, Rod of Harmony, Celestial Star. 
			There's nothing difficult in the first phase; you just need to fly horizontally across the whole world away from all three Primordials; their attacks will never reach you. 
			The only one that can catch up to you is Omnicide, if you hesitate and stop, so be careful. 
			Against Aquaius's tornado attack, a transparent full map will help you; watch his icon closely, and when you see he's stopped, start slowly flying up or down — that's how you survive that attack. 
			Omnicide also has a very simple attack with spinning orbs. The thing is, they always spin in the direction they'll end up going, so you can easily predict which way to fly while they're spinning. 
			The real fun begins in the second phase with the Dream Eater. 
			You can still just fly around the world, but this time you can't predict the tornado, since the Dream Eater stops on several different attacks. 
			There's also one very nasty attack with teleportation and circular movement, which personally I still don't understand how to counter. 
			Generally, if he teleports behind you, you can just wait for him to fly to the other side relative to you, then sharply turn around and fly the other way. 
			Defense is very important in this fight, because their damage and the debuffs they inflict are a horror incarnate. 
			If you get debuffed, the best thing is to immediately cleanse them by equipping and instantly unequipping the Ankh Shield or the {i:ThoriumMod/MantleoftheProtector}Mantle of the Protector (individually these accessories don't cover all of the boss's debuffs, but their combination lets you completely ignore the boss's debuffs altogether). 
			And don't forget about the {i:ThoriumMod/SoulAnchor}Soul Anchor — it can fully heal you once per fight. 
			After defeating this boss, Thorium is considered complete, and all that's left is to craft items from the dropped Essences. For the collection. 
			=====================================================
			Thanks for reading this Infobook tab, which I stretched out over 3 days because of my laziness. Bye-bye.
			'''
	}

	Bestiary: {
		DropsHeader: Drops:
		NoDrops: (no)
		MoreDrops: …and {0} more
